      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of different settings for the suitcase lock where all three digits must be different, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the number of choices for each digit:**\n   - The first digit can be any of the 10 digits: \\(0, 1, 2, \\ldots, 9\\).\n   - The second digit can be any of the remaining 9 digits (since it must be different from the first digit).\n   - The third digit can be any of the remaining 8 digits (since it must be different from the first and second digits).\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of different settings:**\n   - The number of choices for the first digit is 10.\n   - The number of choices for the second digit is 9.\n   - The number of choices for the third digit is 8.\n   \n   Therefore, the total number of different settings is:\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 9 \\times 8\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 9 = 90\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   90 \\times 8 = 720\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of different settings for the suitcase lock is \\(\\boxed{720}\\).",
